remarks.para:
To obtain a supported accessory use the  property and search by name:

foreach (var accessory in ExternalAccessory.EAAccessoryManager.SharedAccessoryManager.ConnectedAccessories)
{
   if (accessory.Name == "Bad Elf GNSS Surveyor")
   {
       return NmeaLocationDataSource.FromAccessory(accessory, "com.bad-elf.gps");
   }
}

It's worth noting that some devices like the Bad Elf GPS requires you to send a message to it to enable NMEA. After starting the location datasource, you can enable it like this:

// Send packet that'll start sending NMEA messages at 1hz:
// see https://github.com/BadElf/gps-sdk/blob/master/README.md#extended-nmea-sentences-with-gsa-and-gsv-satellite-data-and-dop-values for more message types
if (locationDatasource.NmeaDataStream.CanWrite)
    locationDatasource.NmeaDataStream.Write(new byte[] { 0x24, 0xbe, 0x00, 0x11, 0x0b, 0x01, 0x02, 0xff, 0x31, 0x01, 0x32, 0x04, 0x33, 0x02, 0x63, 0x0d, 0x0a });

remarks.code:
var port = new System.IO.Ports.SerialPort("COM1", 9600);
NmeaLocationDataSource serialPortDatasource = NmeaLocationDataSource.FromStreamCreator(
    onStart: (ds) =>
    {
        port.Open();
        return Task.FromResult(port.BaseStream);
    },
    onStop: (ds) =>
    {
        port.Close();
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }
);
MyMapView.LocationDisplay.DataSource = serialPortDatasource;
MyMapView.LocationDisplay.IsEnabled = true; // This will trigger onStart to get called

