member.remarks:
typical usage is to wrap e.g. a OnCollectionChanged call with a using() scope:

        using (BlockReentrancy())
        {
            CollectionChanged(this, new NotifyCollectionChangedEventArgs(action, item, index));
        }

remarks.para:
The local basemap filename must end with .tpk, .tpkx, or .vtpk since these are the supported file
formats. This property can be read directly from settings applied by the author of the online webmap (
) or set by user code to a file known to be on the device.

member.remarks:
The path refers to a .geodatabase file that is used to sync changes to the service specified by
. Each sync process can create an "upload" delta file (
) and/or a "download" delta file ( ).

In some cases, applying updates may require files, such as mobile geodatabases, to be replaced with a new version
requiring the package to be reopened. This property will be true if reopen is required after update;
false otherwise.

